Subject: Throw the `to_propkey2` error in the step's own context

What this does
  - The step handler for `to_propkey2` threw its null-or-undefined TypeError in
    `rf->caller_ctx`. That field is in the frame's record-only tail, which a light frame
    (and every frame a compiled unit builds) does not have: the read took whatever lay past
    the frame, and the throw crashed.
  - It throws in `ctx`, the context the step runs in.

Why we need it
  `h[k]++` with `h` null or undefined, run from a compiled function, crashed instead of
  throwing the TypeError.

--- a/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
+++ b/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
@@ -5776,7 +5776,7 @@
                 if (op == ROP_to_propkey2) {
                     int chk = RD_REG();
                     if (unlikely(JS_IsUndefined(regs[chk]) || JS_IsNull(regs[chk]))) {
-                        JS_ThrowTypeError(rf->caller_ctx, "value has no property");
+                        JS_ThrowTypeError(ctx, "value has no property");
                         goto exception;
                     }
                 }
